### GetFromPos Primitive

The GetFromPos primitive will get a value from source at the given position and assign it to the target.

```text
getFromPos <source> <position> <target>
```
Syntax Structure:
- `Set`:
    * Type: *string*
    * This is the identifier for the instruction.
- `<source>` 
    * Type: *string*
    * This is the name of the participant whose value at position will be read.
- `<position>` 
    * Type: *number*
    * This is the position in the list that will be read.
- `<target>` 
    * Type: *String*
    * This is the name of the participant that will be written to.

#### Example 1:
Gets a book from a basket of books.

```text
create book
getFromPos basket 0 book
```

Pre-transformation state:
```text
    {
        basket: ["Lord of the Rings"],
    }
```

Post-transformation state:
```text
    {
        basket: ["Lord of the Rings"],
        book: "Lord of the Rings",
    }
```
#### Example 2:
Gets the first letter of a string

```text
create first_letter
getFromPos name 0 first_letter
```

Pre-transformation state:
```text
    {
        name: "Lord of the Rings",
    }
```

Post-transformation state:
```text
    {
        name: "Lord of the Rings",
        first_letter: "L",
    }
```